{"from":"4:1","body":"<p><ref to=\"JON.4.1\">1</ref> Jonah repining at God's mercy,<br/><ref to=\"JON.4.4\">4</ref> is reproved by the type of a gourd.<br/><br/><br/><ref to=\"JON.4.9 MAT.20.15 LUK.7.39 LUK.15.28 ACT.13.46 JAS.4.5 JAS.4.6\">4:9; Mt 20:15; Lu 7:39; 15:28; Ac 13:46; Jas 4:5,6</ref></p>"}
{"from":"4:2","body":"<p>he prayed.<br/><ref to=\"1KI.19.4 JER.20.7\">1Ki 19:4; Jer 20:7</ref><br/>I fled.<br/><ref to=\"JON.1.3 LUK.10.29\">1:3; Lu 10:29</ref><br/>thou art.<br/><ref to=\"EXO.34.6 EXO.34.7 NUM.14.18 NUM.14.19 PSA.78.38 PSA.86.5 PSA.86.15 PSA.145.8 HOS.11.8 HOS.11.9\">Ex 34:6,7; Nu 14:18,19; Ps 78:38; 86:5,15; 145:8; Ho 11:8,9</ref><br/><ref to=\"JOL.2.13 JOL.2.14 MIC.7.18\">Joe 2:13,14; Mic 7:18</ref><br/>and of.<br/><ref to=\"JON.3.10 EXO.32.14 PSA.90.13 JER.18.8 AMO.7.3 AMO.7.6\">3:10; Ex 32:14; Ps 90:13; Jer 18:8; Am 7:3,6</ref></p>"}
{"from":"4:3","body":"<p>take.<br/><ref to=\"NUM.11.15 NUM.20.3 1KI.19.4 JOB.3.20 JOB.3.21 JOB.6.8 JOB.6.9 JER.20.14-JER.20.18\">Nu 11:15; 20:3; 1Ki 19:4; Job 3:20,21; 6:8,9; Jer 20:14-18</ref><br/><ref to=\"PHP.1.21-PHP.1.25\">Php 1:21-25</ref><br/>for.<br/><ref to=\"JON.4.8 JOB.7.15 JOB.7.16 ECC.7.1 1CO.9.15\">8; Job 7:15,16; Ec 7:1; 1Co 9:15</ref></p>"}
{"from":"4:4","body":"<p>Doest thou well to be angry? or, Art thou greatly angry?<br/><ref to=\"JON.4.9 NUM.20.11 NUM.20.12 NUM.20.24 PSA.106.32 PSA.106.33 MIC.6.3 MAT.20.15 JAS.1.19 JAS.1.20\">9; Nu 20:11,12,24; Ps 106:32,33; Mic 6:3; Mt 20:15; Jas 1:19,20</ref></p>"}
{"from":"4:5","body":"<p>Jonah.<br/><ref to=\"JON.1.5 1KI.19.9 1KI.19.13 ISA.57.17 JER.20.9\">1:5; 1Ki 19:9,13; Isa 57:17; Jer 20:9</ref><br/>till.<br/><ref to=\"GEN.19.27 GEN.19.28 JER.17.15 JER.17.16 LUK.19.41-LUK.19.44\">Ge 19:27,28; Jer 17:15,16; Lu 19:41-44</ref></p>"}
{"from":"4:6","body":"<p>the Lord.<br/><ref to=\"JON.1.17 PSA.103.10-PSA.103.14\">1:17; Ps 103:10-14</ref><br/>gourd. or, palmcrist. Heb. Kikajon.[Qîyqâyôwn ,] probably the palma Christi, called {kiki,} or {kouki,} by the Egyptians, and {Elkherod} by the Arabs, from which caster oil is extracted. It is as large as the olive tree, has leaves like those of a vine, sometimes as broad as the brim of a hat, and is of very quick growth.<br/>So.<br/><ref to=\"EST.5.9 PRO.23.5 ISA.39.2 AMO.6.13 LUK.10.20 1CO.7.30\">Es 5:9; Pr 23:5; Isa 39:2; Am 6:13; Lu 10:20; 1Co 7:30</ref><br/>was exceeding glad. Heb. rejoiced with great joy.</p>"}
{"from":"4:7","body":"<p>prepared.<br/><ref to=\"JOB.1.21 PSA.30.6 PSA.30.7 PSA.102.10\">Job 1:21; Ps 30:6,7; 102:10</ref><br/>it withered.<br/><ref to=\"PSA.90.5 PSA.90.6 ISA.40.6-ISA.40.8 JOL.1.12\">Ps 90:5,6; Isa 40:6-8; Joe 1:12</ref></p>"}
{"from":"4:8","body":"<p>that God.<br/><ref to=\"JON.4.6 JON.4.7 JON.1.4 JON.1.17 EZK.19.12 REV.3.19\">6,7; 1:4,17; Eze 19:12; Re 3:19</ref><br/>vehement. or, silent. and the sun.<br/><ref to=\"PSA.121.6 SNG.1.6 ISA.49.10 REV.7.16\">Ps 121:6; So 1:6; Isa 49:10; Re 7:16</ref><br/>and wished.<br/><ref to=\"JON.4.3 LEV.10.3 1SA.3.18 2SA.15.25 2SA.15.26 JOB.2.10 PSA.39.9\">3; Le 10:3; 1Sa 3:18; 2Sa 15:25,26; Job 2:10; Ps 39:9</ref></p>"}
{"from":"4:9","body":"<p>Doest thou well to be angry? or, Art thou greatly angry?<br/><ref to=\"JON.4.4\">4</ref><br/>I do well to be angry. or, I am greatly angry.<br/><ref to=\"GEN.4.5-GEN.4.14 JOB.18.4 JOB.40.4 JOB.40.5\">Ge 4:5-14; Job 18:4; 40:4,5</ref><br/>even.<br/><ref to=\"JDG.16.16 JOB.5.2 MAT.26.38 2CO.7.10 REV.9.6\">Jud 16:16; Job 5:2; Mt 26:38; 2Co 7:10; Re 9:6</ref></p>"}
{"from":"4:10","body":"<p>had pity on. or, spared. came up in a night. Heb. was theson of the night.<br/><ref to=\"1SA.20.31 GEN.17.12\">1Sa 20:31; Ge 17:12; *marg:</ref></p>"}
{"from":"4:11","body":"<p>should.<br/><ref to=\"JON.4.1 ISA.1.18 MAT.18.33 LUK.15.28-LUK.15.32\">1; Isa 1:18; Mt 18:33; Lu 15:28-32</ref><br/>Nineveh.<br/><ref to=\"JON.1.2 JON.3.2 JON.3.3\">1:2; 3:2,3</ref><br/>sixscore.It is generally calculated that the young children of any place are a fifth of the inhabitants, and consequently the whole population of Nineveh would amount to about 600,000; which is very inferior to that of London and Paris, though they occupy not one quarter of the ground. In eastern cities there are large vacant spaces for gardens and pasturages, so that there might be very \"much cattle.\"<br/>that cannot.<br/><ref to=\"DEU.1.39\">De 1:39</ref><br/>and also.<br/><ref to=\"PSA.36.6 PSA.104.14 PSA.104.27 PSA.104.28 PSA.145.8 PSA.145.9 PSA.145.15 PSA.145.16\">Ps 36:6; 104:14,27,28; 145:8,9,15,16</ref></p>"}
